### **About Aivres**



Aivres is a leading global data center and cloud computing solutions provider committed to delivering innovative technologies that propel the world’s leading industries to new frontiers. We deliver and deploy robust, performance\-optimized, purpose\-built platforms to major data centers around the globe.



An R\&D project manager is a key person in a research and development project. They are responsible for managing the design, planning, implementation and evaluation of R\&D projects. They are responsible for the success of the project, and for coordinating teams at every stage of the product life\-cycle.


### **Primary Responsibilities**


* Define project objectives and develop a detailed project plan in line with customer requirements;
* Ensure compliance with project deadlines and costs, and manage human and financial resources;
* Manage team members and supervise their work
* Collaborate with other R\&D project managers and support departments to ensure smooth integration of projects;
* Identify potential risks and draw up action plans to counter them;
* Evaluate risks and benefits at each stage of the project and ensure consistency;
* Participate in meetings and lead discussions with customers to define their requirements and expectations;
* Ensure communication between project members and consistency of information;
* Make presentations at events and seminars to promote the project and results;
* Provide updates on progress and problems encountered, ensure the quality of results and propose solutions to problems that may arise.

### **Qualifications**


* Bachelor degree with learning experience in computer science, industry/business management and other related disciplines
* More than 7 years related work experience；
* Independent thinking, teamwork, communication and coordination ability;
* Familiar with x86 project development process, cloud computing, storage, network product structure;
* Strong ability to withstand pressure;
* Experience in server ODM project development is preferred.

### **EEO Statement**



Aivres is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity in our employee population. It is the policy of Aivres to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status or special disabled veteran, marital status, pregnancy, genetic information, or any other legally protected status.


### **Details:**


* **Job Location:** Fremont, California, United States
* **Department:** R\&D
* **Job Type:** Full\-time, on\-site

**How to Apply:**
To apply, please send your resume to ushr@aivres.com.

**Description**
---------------


Under general direction, to plan, organize, direct and control the activities and/or staff of a very large County program.




**The County Executive’s Office (CEO) is responsible for implementing, coordinating, and continuously improving services at the Vietnamese American Service Center (VASC). The mission of the VASC is to address health and social disparities in the Vietnamese and local community. VASC provides integrated health, social, and community services, including primary medical care, dental care, pharmacy, laboratory, behavioral health care, public assistance, and senior nutrition. The center also hosts large\-scale community events, develops core programs, and partners with local organizations to offer educational, wellness, cultural, and community\-building opportunities.**





**This position provides direct oversight of the behavioral clinic and key functions of the center’s core operations. The Program Manager III will directly report to the VASC Director to ensure that the center’s multi\-disciplinary and multi\-departmental operations: a) address critical community needs; b) are effective; c) are culturally and linguistically responsive; and d) are delivered in an integrated, customer\-focused manner.**  



**In addition to meeting the employment standards,** **candidates should possess experience** **in at least three (3\) of the following areas:**  





* **Developing and managing health and/or human services.**
* **Administrative processes such as personnel, policies and procedures, facilities, or budgeting.**
* **Facilitating and maintaining partnerships with diverse community stakeholders and/or multi\-departmental stakeholders.**
* **Developing and implementing strategic outreach, public engagement, and communication strategies, including media relations, public presentations, culturally responsive messaging, and partnerships with community organizations.**




**The candidate should have strong Vietnamese conversational skills to participate in public speaking engagements and must be language certified in Vietnamese, Level I (Speak), or certify prior to the start of assignment, if selected. The candidate should also have the ability to work a flexible schedule to occasionally participate in evening and weekend events and address operational needs.**
**Typical Tasks**
-----------------


* Plans, organizes and directs a County program that provides direct service to the public or other agencies;
* Handles complex coordination between County, local and State resources;
* Prepares staff reports and comprehensive detailed plans with Countywide impact;
* Works closely with cross departmental staff at all levels of the organization;
* Determines program objectives in light of established goals;
* Develops strategies to achieve objectives;
* Establishes program priorities;
* Formulates and implements policies, plans and procedures for carrying out functions of the program;
* Defines personnel resource needs and allocates them as required to reach program objectives;
* Selects and hires staff and ensures the orientation, training and development of program staff;
* Directs and evaluates the work of subordinate staff;
* Establishes an appropriate organizational structure and delineates working level and relationships of personnel to carry out the program's activities;
* Determines budgetary requirements to maintain the program;
* Makes recommendations on the annual budget and may present the program's budget to the Board of Supervisors;
* Is responsible for determining program funding needs and obtaining available outside funding when necessary through grants and/or contracts;
* Is responsible for the implementation, control, monitoring and evaluation of provided services to ensure compliance with terms of received grants and contracts;
* Maintains liaison relationships and represents the program in contacts with public and private agencies and concerned community groups and organizations;
* Prepares reports and correspondence;
* Keeps abreast of new trends and developments related to the program's activities;
* Provides assistance and advice to advisory and planning boards, commissions, task forces and other special groups as required;
* May prepare and make presentations to staff, boards, commissions, and external groups;
* May provide ongoing statistical reports;
* May be assigned as a Disaster Service Worker, as required;
* And performs related duties as required.
**Employment Standards**
------------------------


Sufficient education, training and experience to demonstrate the possession and direct application of the following knowledge and abilities.




**Training and Experience Note:** The required knowledge and abilities are typically attained through training and experience equivalent to possession of a Bachelor's degree. Relevant experience can substitute for education on a year\-for\-year basis. Relevant experience includes experience performing analytical, administrative, lead, supervisory, or management duties, which include interpreting rules and regulations, gathering data and formulating recommendations, and report writing.  





AND


Seven (7\) years of analytical, administrative, lead, supervisory or management experience which includes duties interpreting rules and regulations, gathering data and formulating recommendations, and report writing; four (4\) years of which must be at the journey level.




A Master's degree can substitute for one (1\) year of the required experience.




